# INTERNAL-FILES — single source of truth for repo-only files.
#
# These files live under packages/core/ but must NEVER ship into a consumer's
# .claude/. They only function inside the superkit repo itself (self-audit
# tooling). Listing them once here stops the skip-list from drifting across the
# three call sites that consume it:
#   - lib/installer.js                             (skips them during install)
#   - packages/core/hooks/superkit-counts-verify.sh (subtracts them from shipped counts)
#   - packages/core/hooks/superkit-update.sh        (skips them during update)
#
# Format: one packages/core-relative path per line. Lines starting with '#' and
# blank lines are ignored by parsers. The dirname of each path (hooks/ or rules/)
# selects its category. Never expand this list without evidence.
hooks/superkit-counts-verify.sh
hooks/verify-hooks.sh
rules/superkit-integrity.md
